# Template for devops/grafana/.env -- feeds the `grafana-oauth` secret in the
# `monitoring` namespace:
#
#   cd devops && bash secrets.sh monitoring grafana-oauth grafana/.env
#
# The keys are GF_-prefixed on purpose: the secret is mounted with envFrom
# (grafana.envFromSecret in devops/prometheus/values.yaml), and Grafana maps
# GF_<SECTION>_<KEY> onto grafana.ini. So these two variables ARE the
# [auth.google] client_id / client_secret -- which is why they are not in
# values.yaml, where they would land in a plaintext ConfigMap.
#
# Both values come from a **Google Cloud Console OAuth client that a human
# creates by hand** -- Google has no API for creating "Sign in with Google" web
# clients, so there is nothing to automate here. Full walkthrough, including the
# consent screen and the exact redirect URI:
#   devops/grafana/README.md -> "First-time setup" step 2
#
# Console: Google Auth Platform -> Clients -> the "Grafana (prod)" Web
# application client, in project toixotoixo.
#
# Rotating: create a new secret on that client in the console, put it here,
# re-run secrets.sh, then
# `kubectl rollout restart deployment/prometheus-grafana -n monitoring`.
# Pods do not reload secrets on their own.

GF_AUTH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=__FILL_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID__
GF_AUTH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=__FILL_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET__
